{
  "id": "COMPOUND:23600 - PROTEIN:5782",
  "verbalization": "(+)-Menthol is implicated in the interaction with DMS-273 through a series of molecular pathways involving caspase-5 and 5-Oxobrucine. The evidence suggests that (+)-Menthol acts as a target for 5-Oxobrucine, which in turn targets DMS-273. This relationship is supported by multiple pathways, with caspase-5 serving as a common intermediary in two of the paths. The presence of 5-Oxobrucine as a target of both (+)-Menthol and microtubule-associated protein 1B further highlights a potential role in the signaling cascade. The integration of these pathways suggests that (+)-Menthol may modulate the activity of 5-Oxobrucine, which then affects DMS-273 through a mechanism involving caspase-5. The evidence supports a functional link between (+)-Menthol and DMS-273, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
